illion post-money valuation, co-led by Atreides Management, Mubadala Capital and Valor Equity Partners; Crusoe reported over $140 billion total contracted value and 6 GW+ gross contracted capacity. Bain Capital Ventures lists the company as \"Crusoe Energy\". Country is taken from the Denver dateline of the company's release; no headquarters address was found on its site.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"As the AI factory company, Crusoe is on a mission to accelerate the abundance of energy and intelligence. ... By harnessing large-scale energy sources, building AI-optimized data centers, and delivering a powerful AI cloud platform, Crusoe empowers its customers and partners to build the future faster."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.crusoe.ai/about/company","name":"Crusoe website (company)","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"2018 | Crusoe is founded with an energy-first approach, pioneering technology to convert wasted natural gas into energy for high-performance computing."},"country":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"DENVER – September 17, 2026 – Crusoe, the industry’s first vertically-integrated AI infrastructure provider, today announced..."},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"$140B+ TCV across Crusoe’s vertically-integrated platform serving AI native, hyperscaler, frontier model, and enterprise customers."},"employees":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"All of this is driven by a workforce over 1,800 strong across five countries, including new offices in Bellevue, WA and New York City"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"TPG","status":"current","status_note":"Investor in the Series F round, September 2026","deal_type":"Venture round","value_creation_plan":"The Series F capital will help Crusoe scale its existing programs and support the build out of its own AI factories, from large-scale, vertically-integrated campuses to modular Crusoe Spark units, fueling the rapid growth of Crusoe Cloud.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","notes":"TPG is named among new and existing investors backing the round (co-led by Atreides, Mubadala Capital and Valor). The release does not say which TPG platform invested, so no asset class is recorded. The plan is the company's stated use of proceeds, published on TPG's site."}},{"name":"Crusoe","website":"https://www.crusoe.ai","description":"As the AI factory company, Crusoe provides an energy-first solution for AI infrastructure: harnessing large-scale energy sources, building AI-optimized data centers, and delivering an AI cloud platform (Crusoe Cloud).","sector":"Technology","subsector":"AI infrastructure (AI data centers, energy and GPU cloud)","country":"United States","founded_year":2018,"business_model":"B2B (vertically integrated AI infrastructure: data center capacity and cloud services for AI-native, hyperscaler, frontier model and enterprise customers)","employees":1800,"employees_text":"a workforce over 1,800 strong across five countries","employees_as_of":"2026-09-17","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Chase Lochmiller","title":"Co-founder, CEO and Chairman of the Board of Directors","source_url":"https://www.crusoe.ai/about/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Chase Lochmiller | Co-founder, CEO and Chairman of the Board of Directors"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Michael Gordon","title":"Chief Operating Officer and Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.crusoe.ai/about/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Michael Gordon | Chief Operating Officer and Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"coo","name":"Michael Gordon","title":"Chief Operating Officer and Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.crusoe.ai/about/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Michael Gordon | Chief Operating Officer and Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"other","name":"Cully Cavness","title":"Co-founder, President and Chief Strategy Officer","source_url":"https://www.crusoe.ai/about/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Cully Cavness | Co-founder, President and Chief Strategy Officer"}],"notes":"Series F initial close announced 17 September 2026: anticipated $3.9 billion round at a $30.9 billion post-money valuation, co-led by Atreides Management, Mubadala Capital and Valor Equity Partners; Crusoe reported over $140 billion total contracted value and 6 GW+ gross contracted capacity. Bain Capital Ventures lists the company as \"Crusoe Energy\". Country is taken from the Denver dateline of the company's release; no headquarters address was found on its site.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"As the AI factory company, Crusoe is on a mission to accelerate the abundance of energy and intelligence. ... By harnessing large-scale energy sources, building AI-optimized data centers, and delivering a powerful AI cloud platform, Crusoe empowers its customers and partners to build the future faster."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.crusoe.ai/about/company","name":"Crusoe website (company)","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"2018 | Crusoe is founded with an energy-first approach, pioneering technology to convert wasted natural gas into energy for high-performance computing."},"country":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"DENVER – September 17, 2026 – Crusoe, the industry’s first vertically-integrated AI infrastructure provider, today announced..."},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"$140B+ TCV across Crusoe’s vertically-integrated platform serving AI native, hyperscaler, frontier model, and enterprise customers."},"employees":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/crusoe-raises-3-9-billion-series-f-for-its-vertically-integrated-ai-infrastructure-platform","name":"TPG (Crusoe release)","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"All of this is driven by a workforce over 1,800 strong across five countries, including new offices in Bellevue, WA and New York City"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Bain Capital","status":"current","status_note":"Bain Capital Ventures investor since 2019","asset_class":"Venture capital","deal_type":"Venture round","notes":"Listed in Bain Capital Ventures' portfolio as \"Crusoe Energy\", year of investment 2019: \"Provides sustainable AI cloud computing by using wasted energy to power GPU-optimized data centers.\" Crusoe's own timeline records its Series A in 2019."}},{"name":"AdvanCell","website":"https://www.advancell.com.au","description":"AdvanCell is a vertically integrated, clinical-stage radiopharmaceutical company developing an innovative pipeline of targeted alpha therapies for cancer, built on proprietary Lead-212 technology.","sector":"Life Sciences","subsector":"Radiopharmaceuticals (Lead-212 targeted alpha therapies, oncology)","country":"United States","business_model":"Clinical-stage biotech (drug development; vertically integrated isotope supply and manufacturing)","email":"contact@advancell.com.au","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Philina Lee","title":"Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/news/advancell-appoints-sean-cassidy-as-chief-financial-officer/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"said Philina Lee, Ph.D., Chief Executive Officer, AdvanCell."},{"role":"cfo","name":"Sean Cassidy","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/news/advancell-appoints-sean-cassidy-as-chief-financial-officer/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Boston, USA & Brisbane, Australia – September 15, 2026 – AdvanCell ... today announced the appointment of Sean Cassidy as Chief Financial Officer."}],"notes":"Australian-origin company (site operated by AdvanCell Pty Ltd; offices listed in Brisbane, Richlands, Adelaide and Boston) that established its U.S. global headquarters in Andover, Greater Boston, in June 2026 and describes itself as evolving into a U.S.-based company. Closed an upsized US$315 million Series D on 15 July 2026, led by Ally Bridge Group and co-led by Alpha Wave, with new investors including Bain Capital Life Sciences. Lead program ADVC001 (Lead-212 PSMA-targeted therapy for metastatic prostate cancer) is in Phase 2.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/","name":"AdvanCell website","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"AdvanCell is a vertically integrated, clinical-stage radiopharmaceutical company developing an innovative pipeline of targeted alpha therapies."},"country":{"url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/news/advancell-establishes-us-global-headquarters-and-secures-flagship-manufacturing-facility-in-greater-boston-to-drive-growth-strategy/","name":"AdvanCell news release","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-06-22","evidence":"today announced the establishment of its U.S. Global Headquarters in the Greater Boston area ... The expansion marks an important milestone in the Company’s evolution into a U.S.-based radiopharmaceutical company with integrated operations spanning North America and Australia."},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/news/advancell-closes-us-315-million-oversubscribed-series-d-financing-to-advance-targeted-alpha-therapies-and-expand-clinical-and-commercial-manufacturing-infrastructure/","name":"AdvanCell news release","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-07-15","evidence":"Through its vertically integrated platform spanning proprietary Lead-212 technology, secure isotope supply, advanced manufacturing and clinical development, the Company is unlocking the full potential of targeted alpha therapy."},"email":{"url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/contact/","name":"AdvanCell contact page","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Contact Us | contact@advancell.com.au"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Bain Capital","status":"current","status_note":"New investor in the US$315m Series D, July 2026 (Bain Capital Life Sciences)","asset_class":"Venture capital","deal_type":"Venture round","value_creation_plan":"The Series D proceeds will advance ADVC001 toward Phase 3 development in metastatic prostate cancer, expand AdvanCell's proprietary Lead-212 platform, isotope supply and U.S. manufacturing infrastructure, and accelerate its pipeline of targeted alpha therapies.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.advancell.com.au/news/advancell-closes-us-315-million-oversubscribed-series-d-financing-to-advance-targeted-alpha-therapies-and-expand-clinical-and-commercial-manufacturing-infrastructure/","notes":"Bain Capital Life Sciences participated as a new investor; the round was led by Ally Bridge Group and co-led by Alpha Wave. The plan is the company's stated use of proceeds, not a Bain Capital statement."}},{"name":"Australian Venue Co","website":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au","description":"Australian Venue Co is behind many of the country’s best-loved pubs, bars and venues, operating more than 200 venues across Australia and New Zealand with a local-first approach supported by a centralised head office.","sector":"Consumer/Retail","subsector":"Hospitality (pubs, bars, hotels and function venues)","country":"Australia","business_model":"B2C (owner-operator of licensed pubs, bars and venues)","email":"info@ausvenueco.com.au","email_type":"generic","employees":8300,"employees_text":"We employ more than 8,300 employees across the country","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Paul Waterson","title":"Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/our-team/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Meet the team | Paul Waterson | Chief Executive Officer"},{"role":"cfo","name":"David Noonan","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/our-team/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"David Noonan | Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"coo","name":"Craig Ellison","title":"Chief Operating Officer","source_url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/our-team/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Craig Ellison | Chief Operating Officer"}],"notes":"Head office 16/242 Exhibition St, Melbourne VIC 3000. CVC's release (1 August 2025) says AVC operated 243 licensed venues, primarily pubs, plus some bars and licensed restaurants across Australia and New Zealand. Ownership after the deal: PAG 45%, CVC Capital Partners Asia VI 45%, management the remainder. The employee figure carries no date on the company's About page.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/about/","name":"Australian Venue Co website (About)","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"From landmark institutions to humble locals, Australian Venue Co is behind many of the country’s best-loved pubs, bars and venues. ... Operating more than 200 venues from coast to coast, Australian Venue Co takes a local-first approach to our venues while providing specialist support at scale from our centralised head office."},"country":{"url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/contact/","name":"Australian Venue Co contact page","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"16/242 Exhibition St, Melbourne VIC 3000"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2025/cvc-joins-pag-to-partner-with-australian-venue-co-in-new-era-of-growth/","name":"CVC news release","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2025-08-01","evidence":"AVC, which currently operates 243 licensed venues, primarily pubs, as well as some bars and licensed restaurants across Australia and New Zealand."},"email":{"url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/contact/","name":"Australian Venue Co contact page","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"& general enquiries | 16/242 Exhibition St, Melbourne VIC 3000 | 1800 836 837 | info@ausvenueco.com.au"},"employees":{"url":"https://www.ausvenueco.com.au/about/","name":"Australian Venue Co website (About)","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"We employ more than 8,300 employees across the country and help turn jobs into rewarding hospitality careers."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"CVC Capital Partners","status":"current","status_note":"CVC Capital Partners Asia VI acquired a 45% stake from PAG in August 2025 (joint control with PAG)","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Minority stake","value_creation_plan":"CVC and PAG as owners will allow the company to revamp existing premises and deliver better customer experience while also funding new opportunities in major population centres; CVC said it will partner with management and PAG to support the next phase of growth for AVC.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2025/cvc-joins-pag-to-partner-with-australian-venue-co-in-new-era-of-growth/","notes":"Announced 1 August 2025 (the batch gives 2026 as the invested year; CVC's release is dated 2025). Stake bought from majority owner PAG; PAG and CVC Capital Partners Asia VI each hold 45%, management the remainder."}},{"name":"Japan Wellbeing Corp","description":"Japan Wellbeing Corp. (JWB) is one of the largest providers of home care services in Japan: the holding company of Tsukui Corporation and SOYOKAZE, offering day care, short-stay residential care, group homes, in-home nursing and care management through more than 1,100 locations serving about 110,000 users a month.","sector":"Healthcare","subsector":"Elderly home care and nursing care services","country":"Japan","founded_year":2024,"business_model":"B2C (home and residential care services for elderly users)","leaders":[{"role":"other","name":"高畠 毅","title":"代表者 (Representative), 株式会社ツクイ (Tsukui Corporation, JWB subsidiary)","source_url":"https://prtimes.jp/main/html/rd/p/000000128.000049667.html","source_kind":"wire","evidence":"株式会社ツクイ ... 代表者名 高畠　毅 ... 設立 1969年06月"}],"notes":"JWB was established in 2024 as the holding company for Tsukui (founded 1969; care business since 1983) and SOYOKAZE (care business since 1997, formerly Unimat Retirement Community); the group has 16 care-related subsidiaries. Headquartered in Tokyo and Kanagawa (Tsukui's head office: Kounan-ku, Yokohama). No JWB-level CEO or CFO was named on any page opened; the Tsukui representative's name is given only in Japanese on the source page. Advent did not disclose terms; Nikkei Asia's headline put the deal at about $1bn.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.adventinternational.com/news/advent-announces-first-japan-investment-with-acquisition-of-japan-wellbeing-corp/","name":"Advent International press release","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-06-25","evidence":"Japan Wellbeing Corp. (JWB) is one of the largest providers of home care services in Japan ... JWB offers a comprehensive suite of services including day care, short-stay residential care, group homes, in-home nursing and care management. Headquartered in Tokyo and Kanagawa, the company operates more than 1,100 locations across Japan and serves approximately 110,000 users each month."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://prtimes.jp/main/html/rd/p/000000128.000049667.html","name":"PR Times (JWB / Tsukui / SOYOKAZE notice)","kind":"wire","as_of":"2026-06-25","evidence":"2024年のツクイとSOYOKAZEのホールディングカンパニーとしてのJWB設立"},"country":{"url":"https://www.adventinternational.com/news/advent-announces-first-japan-investment-with-acquisition-of-japan-wellbeing-corp/","name":"Advent International press release","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-06-25","evidence":"Headquartered in Tokyo and Kanagawa, the company operates more than 1,100 care locations"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.adventinternational.com/news/advent-announces-first-japan-investment-with-acquisition-of-japan-wellbeing-corp/","name":"Advent International press release","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-06-25","evidence":"the company operates more than 1,100 care locations and serves approximately 110,000 users each month."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Advent International","status":"current","status_note":"Agreed June 2026 to acquire from MBK Partners; closing expected Q3 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Secondary buyout","value_creation_plan":"Advent will partner with JWB's management team to support the company's next phase of growth through targeted facility expansion, extending its national reach, and through investment in staff development, operational best practices, and technology to improve the standard of care.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.adventinternational.com/news/advent-announces-first-japan-investment-with-acquisition-of-japan-wellbeing-corp/","notes":"Advent's first investment in Japan; seller MBK Partners. Terms not disclosed by Advent; Nikkei Asia (25 June 2026) headlined the deal at $1bn and said Advent aims to add efficiency through AI and consolidation."}},{"name":"Acclime","website":"https://www.acclime.com","description":"Acclime is a leading professional services firm providing integrated corporate services, fund services, accounting, tax, and advisory solutions across Asia Pacific and the Middle East.","sector":"Business Services, Financial Services","subsector":"Corporate services (accounting, tax, HR and payroll, fund services, corporate secretarial, risk and advisory)","country":"Hong Kong","founded_year":2019,"business_model":"B2B (professional and corporate services to multinationals' subsidiaries, regional businesses, funds, family offices and private capital firms)","employees":2000,"employees_text":"With over 2,000 professionals operating as one unified firm across 18 markets","employees_as_of":"2025-12-18","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Izzy Silva","title":"Group Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.manilatimes.net/2025/12/18/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/warburg-pincus-signs-agreement-to-invest-in-acclime-a-leading-tech-forward-corporate-and-business-services-provider-in-asia-pacific/2245773/amp","source_kind":"wire","evidence":"As part of its evolution into a scaled, multi-market platform, Acclime appointed Izzy Silva as Group Chief Executive Officer in early 2024."},{"role":"other","name":"Martin Crawford","title":"Founder and Chairman","source_url":"https://www.manilatimes.net/2025/12/18/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/warburg-pincus-signs-agreement-to-invest-in-acclime-a-leading-tech-forward-corporate-and-business-services-provider-in-asia-pacific/2245773/amp","source_kind":"wire","evidence":"Martin Crawford , Founder and Chairman of Acclime , said: ..."}],"notes":"Founded in 2019 by Martin Crawford and Debby Davidson; more than 50 acquisitions since founding, 18 markets, over 17,000 clients, 60+ partners; proprietary AI-enabled automation platform Aura. Reuters (17 December 2025, via MarketScreener) described it as Hong Kong-based and reported the deal would value Acclime at between $950 million and $1 billion. Acclime's own website blocked automated access, so no contact email is recorded.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.manilatimes.net/2025/12/18/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/warburg-pincus-signs-agreement-to-invest-in-acclime-a-leading-tech-forward-corporate-and-business-services-provider-in-asia-pacific/2245773/amp","name":"PR Newswire release (Warburg Pincus), syndicated","kind":"wire","as_of":"2025-12-18","evidence":"Acclime is a leading professional services firm providing integrated corporate services, fund services, accounting, tax, and advisory solutions across Asia Pacific and the Middle East ."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://warburgpincus.com/investments/acclime/","name":"Warburg Pincus portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Founded in 2019, Acclime is a leading APAC corporate services specialist"},"country":{"url":"https://uk.marketscreener.com/news/warburg-pincus-to-invest-in-hong-kong-s-acclime-ce7d50dfd88ff121","name":"Reuters via MarketScreener","kind":"press","as_of":"2025-12-17","evidence":"Hong Kong-based corporate and business services firm Acclime"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.manilatimes.net/2025/12/18/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/warburg-pincus-signs-agreement-to-invest-in-acclime-a-leading-tech-forward-corporate-and-business-services-provider-in-asia-pacific/2245773/amp","name":"PR Newswire release (Warburg Pincus), syndicated","kind":"wire","as_of":"2025-12-18","evidence":"The firm today serves over 17,000 clients-including subsidiaries of multinational corporations expanding into Asia Pacific , regional businesses, family offices, private capital firms, and high-growth companies"},"employees":{"url":"https://www.manilatimes.net/2025/12/18/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/warburg-pincus-signs-agreement-to-invest-in-acclime-a-leading-tech-forward-corporate-and-business-services-provider-in-asia-pacific/2245773/amp","name":"PR Newswire release (Warburg Pincus), syndicated","kind":"wire","as_of":"2025-12-18","evidence":"With over 2,000 professionals operating as one unified firm across 18 markets, Acclime serves a diverse range of private clients, regional enterprises, multinationals, funds, and family offices."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Warburg Pincus","status":"current","status_note":"Buyout agreed December 2025; Warburg lists investment year 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Buyout","value_creation_plan":"Warburg Pincus seeks to leverage its global track record in building leading business services platforms to support Acclime's next phase of growth, international expansion, and innovation, partnering with management to accelerate growth, expand capabilities, and create long-term value.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.manilatimes.net/2025/12/18/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/warburg-pincus-signs-agreement-to-invest-in-acclime-a-leading-tech-forward-corporate-and-business-services-provider-in-asia-pacific/2245773/amp","notes":"Warburg Pincus portfolio page: Area of Focus Business Services, Financial Services; Geography Asia; Stage Buyout; Investment Year 2026. Stem Financial were foundational investors. Reuters reported a valuation of $950m-$1bn."}},{"name":"Dayforce","website":"https://www.dayforce.com","description":"Dayforce is a global human capital management (HCM) software company whose single AI-powered people platform covers HR, Pay, Time, Talent, and Analytics.","sector":"Software","subsector":"Human capital management (HCM) cloud software: HR, payroll, workforce management","country":"United States","founded_year":1992,"business_model":"B2B subscription/SaaS (cloud HCM; recurring revenue plus professional services)","email":"mediainquiries@dayforce.com","email_type":"press","employees":9600,"employees_text":"As of December 31, 2024, we had more than 9,600 employees globally.","employees_as_of":"2024-12-31","revenue":1760000000,"revenue_currency":"USD","revenue_period":"FY2024","ebitda":501500000,"ebitda_currency":"USD","ebitda_period":"FY2024","ebitda_basis":"adjusted","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"David Ossip","title":"CEO and Founder","source_url":"https://www.dayforce.com/who-we-are/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"David Ossip | CEO and Founder | David Ossip is CEO and Founder at Dayforce."},{"role":"cfo","name":"Jeremy Johnson","title":"Executive Vice President, Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.dayforce.com/who-we-are/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Jeremy Johnson | Executive Vice President, Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"coo","name":"Steve Holdridge","title":"President and Chief Operating Officer","source_url":"https://www.dayforce.com/who-we-are/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Steve Holdridge | President and Chief Operating Officer"}],"notes":"Formerly Ceridian HCM Holding. Taken private by Thoma Bravo for approximately US$12.3 billion (US$70.00 per share in cash); completed 4 February 2026 and delisted from the NYSE and TSX. No FY2025 10-K was filed, so the latest audited full-year figures are FY2024 (10-K filed 28 February 2025). Adjusted EBITDA is the company's non-GAAP measure (28.5% margin). Corporate headquarters Minneapolis, Minnesota, with a major office in Toronto.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017025029980/day-20241231.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2024","kind":"filing","as_of":"2025-02-28","evidence":"Dayforce, Inc. is a global human capital management (“HCM”) software company. Dayforce, our flagship Cloud HCM platform, provides a full suite of HCM functionality, including global human resources (“HR”), payroll and tax, workforce management, benefits, and talent intelligence functionality."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.thomabravo.com/portfolio/dayforce","name":"Thoma Bravo portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"CEO David Ossip | Platform Flagship | HQ Minneapolis, MN, and Toronto, ON | Sector Applications | Year Invested 2026 | Year Founded 1992"},"country":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017025029980/day-20241231.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2024","kind":"filing","as_of":"2025-02-28","evidence":"Our corporate headquarters is located in Minneapolis, Minnesota and we also have a major office location in Toronto, Ontario, Canada"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017025029980/day-20241231.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2024","kind":"filing","as_of":"2025-02-28","evidence":"Total recurring 1,517.3 ... Professional services and other 242.7 ... Total revenue 1,760.0 (in millions, 2024)"},"email":{"url":"https://www.dayforce.com/who-we-are/newsroom","name":"Dayforce newsroom","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Contact us to speak with our media relations team. mediainquiries@dayforce.com"},"employees":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017025029980/day-20241231.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2024","kind":"filing","as_of":"2024-12-31","evidence":"As of December 31, 2024, we had more than 9,600 employees globally."},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017025029980/day-20241231.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2024","kind":"filing","as_of":"2024-12-31","evidence":"Total revenue increased $246.3 million, or 16.3%, to $1,760.0 million for the year ended December 31, 2024"},"ebitda":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017025029980/day-20241231.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2024","kind":"filing","as_of":"2024-12-31","evidence":"Adjusted EBITDA (a) (in millions) $ 501.5 $ 410.2 Adjusted EBITDA margin (a) 28.5 % 27.1 %"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Thoma Bravo","status":"current","status_note":"Taken private by Thoma Bravo, completed February 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Take-private","value_creation_plan":"As a private company, Dayforce is to accelerate growth, customer value, and AI leadership in HCM; Thoma Bravo said it sees significant opportunity to help Dayforce expand its reach and unlock its next phase of growth and customer impact.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000114036126003628/ef20064744_ex99-2.htm","notes":"Agreement announced 21 August 2025; approved by stockholders 12 November 2025; closed 4 February 2026 for approximately US$12.3 billion. Thoma Bravo lists Dayforce as a Flagship platform investment."}},{"name":"Nexthink","website":"https://nexthink.com","description":"Nexthink is the leader in digital employee experience (DEX) management software, giving IT leaders insight to see, diagnose and fix issues at scale impacting employees anywhere, with any application or network, before employees notice.","sector":"Software","subsector":"IT operations / digital employee experience (DEX) management","country":"United States","business_model":"B2B enterprise software (sold to IT organisations; more than 1,500 enterprise customers)","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Pedro Bados","title":"Co-Founder & CEO","source_url":"https://nexthink.com/company/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Meet our leadership team | Pedro Bados | Co-Founder & CEO"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Hamza Benamar","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://nexthink.com/company/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Hamza Benamar | Chief Financial Officer"}],"notes":"Dual headquartered in Lausanne, Switzerland and Boston, Massachusetts, with 9 offices worldwide; Vista's portfolio page gives the headquarters as Boston, MA, which is the country recorded here. Serves more than 1,500 enterprise customers and 25 million employees. Vista agreed a majority investment on 27 October 2025 valuing the company at approximately $3 billion; Vista lists the investment year as 2026 and status Current. The leadership page lists no COO.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/vista-equity-partners-to-make-majority-investment-in-nexthink-valuing-the-company-at-approximately-3-billion-302595273.html","name":"PR Newswire (Nexthink release)","kind":"wire","as_of":"2025-10-27","evidence":"Nexthink is the leader in digital employee experience management software. The company provides IT leaders with unprecedented insight allowing them to see, diagnose and fix issues at scale impacting employees anywhere, with any application or network, before employees notice the issue."},"country":{"url":"https://www.vistaequitypartners.com/company/nexthink/","name":"Vista Equity Partners portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Year of Investment 2026 | Status Current | Headquarters Boston, MA | Strategy Flagship | Industry IT Operations"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/vista-equity-partners-to-make-majority-investment-in-nexthink-valuing-the-company-at-approximately-3-billion-302595273.html","name":"PR Newswire (Nexthink release)","kind":"wire","as_of":"2025-10-27","evidence":"serving more than 1,500 enterprise customers and 25 million employees globally"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Vista Equity Partners","status":"current","status_note":"Majority investment by Vista's Flagship fund; agreed October 2025, Vista lists 2026 as investment year","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Buyout","value_creation_plan":"Vista said it is excited to partner with Nexthink as it continues to lead the expansion of the DEX market, with the investment set to accelerate Nexthink's innovation and unlock a new era of AI-powered, agentic Digital Employee Experience; founder and CEO Pedro Bados and the leadership team continue to lead the company.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/vista-equity-partners-to-make-majority-investment-in-nexthink-valuing-the-company-at-approximately-3-billion-302595273.html","notes":"Valuation approximately $3 billion; closing was expected in Q1 2026. Vista portfolio page: Strategy Flagship, Status Current."}},{"name":"Electronic Arts","website":"https://www.ea.com","description":"Electronic Arts is a global leader in digital interactive entertainment, building games and experiences that grow the global online communities around its key franchises and intellectual property.","sector":"Content & Entertainment","subsector":"Video games (console, PC and mobile; full games and live services)","country":"United States","business_model":"B2C (full game sales plus live services and other in-game revenue)","employees":14600,"employees_text":"As of March 31, 2026, we employed approximately 14,600 people globally","employees_as_of":"2026-03-31","revenue":7531000000,"revenue_currency":"USD","revenue_period":"FY2026 (12 months to 2026-03-31)","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Andrew Wilson","title":"Chief Executive Officer, Chair of the Board","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","source_kind":"filing","evidence":"Name Age Position Andrew Wilson 51 Chief Executive Officer, Chair of the Board (executive officers as of May 11, 2026)"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Stuart Canfield","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","source_kind":"filing","evidence":"Stuart Canfield 47 Chief Financial Officer ... Mr. Canfield has served as EA’s Chief Financial Officer since June 2023"},{"role":"other","name":"Laura Miele","title":"President of EA Entertainment & Central Development","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","source_kind":"filing","evidence":"Laura Miele 56 President of EA Entertainment & Central Development"}],"notes":"Acquired by a consortium of PIF, Silver Lake and Affinity Partners at $210 per share in cash; agreement announced 29 September 2025, approved by stockholders 22 December 2025, closed per 8-K filed 4 August 2026, and delisted from NASDAQ. FY2026 (to 31 March 2026): net revenue $7,531m, operating income $1,162m. EBITDA is not recorded because the cash flow statement combines depreciation and amortization with accretion and impairment ($323m). Principal executive offices: 209 Redwood Shores Parkway, Redwood City, California.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.silverlake.com/portfolio/electronic-arts/","name":"Silver Lake portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Electronic Arts is a global leader in digital interactive entertainment. The company is focused on building games and experiences that grow the global online communities around its key franchises and intellectual property"},"country":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-05-11","evidence":"Our principal executive offices are located at 209 Redwood Shores Parkway, Redwood City, California 94065"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-03-31","evidence":"Net revenue: Full game downloads $ 1,708 ... Packaged goods 440 ... Full game $ 2,148 ... Live services and other $ 5,383 ... Total net revenue $ 7,531"},"employees":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-03-31","evidence":"As of March 31, 2026, we employed approximately 14,600 people globally, with 71 percent located internationally."},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000162828026033617/ea-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-03-31","evidence":"Our key financial results for our fiscal year ended March 31, 2026 were as follows: • Total net revenue was $7,531 million, up 1 percent year-over-year."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Silver Lake","status":"current","status_note":"Take-private by PIF, Silver Lake and Affinity Partners, completed 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Take-private","value_creation_plan":"Silver Lake said it is proud to join PIF and Affinity Partners to invest heavily in EA's growth, including what AI can do to enhance game development and player experience, and to partner with Andrew Wilson and the EA team.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/712515/000114036126031157/ef20079099_ex99-1.htm","notes":"Silver Lake portfolio page: Partner Since 2026; Strategy Silver Lake Partners & Alpine; Current Investment. Consortium paid $210 per share in cash; PIF had been a minority investor for more than five years."}},{"name":"Ode","website":"https://www.ode.com","description":"Ode with Anthropic is an AI services company that combines Anthropic’s frontier AI models with a team of experienced AI engineers to help organizations identify where AI can have the greatest impact, and then build the systems that deliver it.","sector":"Information, Content & Business Services","subsector":"Enterprise AI transformation services (forward-deployed engineering)","country":"United States","founded_year":2026,"business_model":"B2B services (AI transformation programs for enterprises)","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Chris Taylor","title":"CEO","source_url":"https://www.ode.com/press/anthropic-blackstone-and-hellman-friedman-introduce-ode-with-anthropic-an-enterprise-ai-services-firm","source_kind":"company","evidence":"The company is led by Chris Taylor as CEO and Eddie Siegel as CTO, who co-founded Fractional AI and held those same roles there."},{"role":"other","name":"Eddie Siegel","title":"CTO","source_url":"https://www.ode.com/press/anthropic-blackstone-and-hellman-friedman-introduce-ode-with-anthropic-an-enterprise-ai-services-firm","source_kind":"company","evidence":"The company is led by Chris Taylor as CEO and Eddie Siegel as CTO"}],"notes":"Launched under the Ode with Anthropic name on 15 July 2026 (San Francisco) by Anthropic, Blackstone and Hellman & Friedman, with an investor consortium including Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC and Sequoia Capital. Built on Fractional AI, the applied AI services firm acquired in May 2026; later acquired Casper Studios. The press contact on the release is a PR agency address, so no company email is recorded.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.ode.com/press/anthropic-blackstone-and-hellman-friedman-introduce-ode-with-anthropic-an-enterprise-ai-services-firm","name":"Ode press release","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-07-15","evidence":"Ode with Anthropic is an AI services company launched in 2026 ... Ode combines Anthropic’s frontier AI models with a team of experienced AI engineers to help organizations identify where AI can have the greatest impact, and then build the systems that deliver it."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.ode.com/press/anthropic-blackstone-and-hellman-friedman-introduce-ode-with-anthropic-an-enterprise-ai-services-firm","name":"Ode press release","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-07-15","evidence":"Ode with Anthropic is an AI services company launched in 2026 through a partnership between Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, and a consortium of global investors"},"country":{"url":"https://www.ode.com/press/anthropic-blackstone-and-hellman-friedman-introduce-ode-with-anthropic-an-enterprise-ai-services-firm","name":"Ode press release","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-07-15","evidence":"San Francisco, CA – July 15, 2026 – Today, Anthropic, Blackstone, and Hellman & Friedman introduced Ode with Anthropic (“Ode”)"},"business_model":{"url":"https://hf.com/portfolio/ode-with-anthropic-ode/","name":"Hellman & Friedman portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Ode brings together senior Anthropic Applied AI leadership and world-class forward deployed engineering talent to deliver high-impact AI transformation programs to enterprises."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Hellman & Friedman","status":"current","status_note":"Founding investor in a newly formed company, 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","value_creation_plan":"H&F invested in Ode, a newly formed company focused on AI transformation services, purpose-built to accelerate enterprise AI deployment at scale by bringing together senior Anthropic Applied AI leadership and forward deployed engineering talent.","value_creation_source_url":"https://hf.com/portfolio/ode-with-anthropic-ode/","notes":"Founding partner alongside Anthropic and Blackstone. No deal type recorded: a founding equity investment in a new company does not fit the buyout or venture categories, and no stake size was disclosed."}},{"name":"Columbus McKinnon","website":"https://www.cmco.com/","description":"Columbus McKinnon is a worldwide designer, manufacturer and marketer of intelligent motion solutions that efficiently and ergonomically move, lift, position, and secure materials; key products include hoists, crane components, precision conveyor systems, rigging tools, light rail workstations, and digital power and motion control systems.","sector":"Industrials & Business Services","subsector":"Material handling equipment (hoists, rigging, crane components, conveyance, motion control)","country":"United States","founded_year":1875,"business_model":"B2B (designs, manufactures and sells material handling products for commercial and industrial customers)","employees":7300,"employees_text":"As of March 31, 2026, we had approximately 7,300 employees globally.","employees_as_of":"2026-03-31","revenue":1193451000,"revenue_currency":"USD","revenue_period":"FY2026 (12 months to 2026-03-31)","ebitda":181400000,"ebitda_currency":"USD","ebitda_period":"FY2026 (12 months to 2026-03-31)","ebitda_basis":"adjusted","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"David J. Wilson","title":"President, Chief Executive Officer and Director","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000022/cmco-20260331.htm","source_kind":"filing","evidence":"/s/ David J. Wilson President, Chief Executive Officer and Director (Principal Executive Officer) June 8, 2026"},{"role":"cfo","name":"John R. Linker","title":"Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000048/cmco-20260731.htm","source_kind":"filing","evidence":"on July 1, 2026, the board of directors of Columbus McKinnon Corporation (the “Company”) appointed John R. Linker, age 51, as the Company’s new Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer ... Mr. Linker began his appointment as the Company’s principal financial officer as of July 31, 2026."}],"notes":"Nasdaq-listed (CMCO); corporate headquarters Charlotte, North Carolina. Completed the acquisition of Kito Crosby from KKR funds on 3 February 2026, so FY2026 includes about two months of Kito Crosby; FY2026 also includes a $103.3m gain on the divestiture of U.S. power chain hoist and chain operations and a $200.0m goodwill impairment. Adjusted EBITDA is the company's non-GAAP measure (15.2% margin). Prior CFO Gregory P. Rustowicz separated on 1 July 2026. FY27 guidance: net sales $2.05-2.12bn, adjusted EBITDA $390-410m.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.cdr.com/portfolio/columbus-mckinnon","name":"CD&R portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Columbus McKinnon is a worldwide designer, manufacturer and marketer of intelligent motion solutions that move the world forward and improve lives by efficiently and ergonomically moving, lifting, positioning, and securing materials. Key products include hoists, crane components, precision conveyor systems, rigging tools, light rail workstations, and digital power and motion control systems."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000022/cmco-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-06-08","evidence":"Founded in 1875, Columbus McKinnon Corporation ..."},"country":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000022/cmco-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-06-08","evidence":"We maintain our corporate headquarters in Charlotte, NC (a leased property)"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.cdr.com/portfolio/columbus-mckinnon","name":"CD&R portfolio page","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"The Company is focused on commercial and industrial applications that require the safety and quality provided by its superior design and engineering know-how."},"employees":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000022/cmco-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-03-31","evidence":"As of March 31, 2026, we had approximately 7,300 employees globally."},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000022/cmco-20260331.htm","name":"SEC Form 10-K FY2026","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-03-31","evidence":"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS Year Ended March 31, 2026 ... (In thousands) Net sales $ 1,193,451"},"ebitda":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000100522926000017/exhibit9913312026.htm","name":"Columbus McKinnon FY2026 results release (8-K Ex. 99.1)","kind":"filing","as_of":"2026-06-04","evidence":"Adjusted EBITDA 4 of $181.4 million with Adjusted EBITDA Margin 4 of 15.2%, including tariff and unfavorable product sales mix impacts (full year fiscal 2026)"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Clayton, Dubilier & Rice, LLC","status":"current","status_note":"$800m convertible preferred investment (about 43% as-converted), issued at the Kito Crosby closing in February 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"PIPE","value_creation_plan":"CD&R's investment financed part of the Kito Crosby acquisition, which the company expects to scale the business, deliver improved Adjusted EBITDA Margin and enhance shareholder value through $70 million of expected net annual run rate cost synergies; in connection with the investment the board was expanded from 9 to 12 directors with Michael Lamach, Nate Sleeper and Andrew Campelli.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1005229/000119312526037694/d54396dex991.htm","notes":"800,000 Series A Cumulative Convertible Participating Preferred Shares issued to CD&R XII Keystone Holdings, L.P. under an investment agreement dated 10 February 2025; initial conversion price $37.68, about 43% of common stock on an as-converted basis at issuance; right to designate up to three directors. The plan is the company's statement about the acquisition CD&R helped finance."}}]$pp$::jsonb);
